  "takeaway": "Systemic pressure increased into the end of July as long-term Treasury yields reached multi-year highs, the BOJ maintained a hawkish normalization bias, and commercial real-estate delinquencies rose sharply. High-yield spreads remain contained and labor markets remain resilient, so a broad credit event has not begun. Extreme insider selling, elevated AI valuations, private-credit stress and deteriorating consumer credit argue for maintaining liquidity and preparing for dislocations rather than deploying aggressively.",
